Two versions of the same tool definition, both syntactically valid:

**A:**
```json
{
  "name": "search",
  "description": "Searches.",
  "input_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"q": {"type": "string"}}}
}
```

**B:**
```json
{
  "name": "search_internal_docs",
  "description": "Search the company's internal engineering wiki (Confluence) for existing documentation. Use this before writing new documentation, to check whether something similar already exists. Does NOT search the public internet or the codebase — use search_codebase for source files.",
  "input_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"q": {"type": "string", "description": "Keywords, not a full sentence — e.g. 'deployment rollback procedure'."}}}
}
```

